WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.628
Hello, colleagues,
students, and friends!

00:00:04.045 --> 00:00:05.964
I hope you are having
a wonderful start

00:00:05.964 --> 00:00:07.424
to the fall semester.

00:00:08.049 --> 00:00:10.802
As I was preparing for the
new academic year,

00:00:10.802 --> 00:00:13.263
which is my 11th as president,

00:00:13.263 --> 00:00:16.099
I reflected on all that
we've achieved together

00:00:16.099 --> 00:00:17.392
over the past decade.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:20.478
And I considered
when would be a good time

00:00:20.478 --> 00:00:23.106
for a leadership
transition here at Yale.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:26.443
Of course,
we have so much more to do,

00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:28.945
so there really is no perfect
time for one.

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:31.948
But right now,
we are a strong university,

00:00:31.948 --> 00:00:35.493
and we've built momentum
for even greater achievement

00:00:35.493 --> 00:00:37.245
in the years ahead.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:41.249
So, I decided that this will be
my last year as president.

00:00:41.624 --> 00:00:45.587
I will step down from the role
on June 30th, 2024,

00:00:45.587 --> 00:00:48.506
unless additional time is
needed to choose a successor.

00:00:49.132 --> 00:00:51.968
I will return to research,
writing, and, eventually,

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:54.971
teaching in Yale's
Department of Psychology.

00:00:55.263 --> 00:00:58.183
So, you will
certainly see me around campus.

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:01.603
Of course, it's been an honor
and a privilege

00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:04.063
to serve our university
and community.

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:07.025
After all,
I've been here for 42 years.

00:01:07.275 --> 00:01:10.278
And I'm profoundly proud of the
progress we have made

00:01:10.278 --> 00:01:13.114
to advance Yale's mission of
education, research,

00:01:13.114 --> 00:01:17.494
scholarship, preservation,
and practice.

00:01:17.494 --> 00:01:20.789
We've added over 2.2 million
square feet of stunning

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:23.792
and functional space
for research and teaching —

00:01:23.875 --> 00:01:26.753
including the Humanities
Quadrangle,

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:29.756
Yale Science Building, Kline
Tower, Peabody Museum,

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:31.716
two new residential colleges,

00:01:31.716 --> 00:01:35.136
the Schwarzman Center,
and so much more.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.806
We've transformed and are
continuing to transform

00:01:37.806 --> 00:01:41.559
Science Hill, enhanced
multidisciplinary scholarship

00:01:41.559 --> 00:01:44.979
across the university, and
created institutes and centers

00:01:44.979 --> 00:01:48.525
for research in the humanities,
sciences, social science,

00:01:48.525 --> 00:01:49.901
and engineering.

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:52.904
We launched the Jackson
School of Global Affairs,

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:56.074
and we are transitioning
the Yale School of Public Health

00:01:56.074 --> 00:01:58.743
and the School of Engineering
and Applied Science

00:01:58.743 --> 00:02:00.620
into independent schools.

00:02:00.995 --> 00:02:05.458
At the same time, we’ve fostered
a greater culture of innovation

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:09.671
Good examples are the creation
of Yale Ventures and Tsai CITY —

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.966
and nurtured increased
international partnerships

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.676
through the
Yale Africa Initiative

00:02:14.676 --> 00:02:18.096
and other faculty-led
collaborations worldwide.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:22.350
And here at home, we've
established university-wide

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:26.396
efforts on inclusion,
diversity, and belonging.

00:02:26.771 --> 00:02:29.941
This year we will finish a
project focused on understanding

00:02:29.941 --> 00:02:33.486
Yale's historical roles in
and associations with slavery.

00:02:33.945 --> 00:02:36.489
Meanwhile, we strengthen
partnerships

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:39.659
with and financial support
for our home city,

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:42.787
creating opportunities
for inclusive growth.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:46.666
We also have expanded the
faculty across the university,

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:49.502
and we've improved the
excellence and breadth

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:51.462
of faculty research
and scholarship.

00:02:51.754 --> 00:02:55.174
And the student body doesn't
look at all like it did

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:58.011
a decade ago — it is
now even more promising

00:02:58.011 --> 00:03:01.556
and diverse across every
dimension thanks to

00:03:01.556 --> 00:03:04.767
greater affordability for
undergraduate, graduate,

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:06.853
and professional
school students.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.607
For example, we expanded
the undergraduate student body

00:03:10.607 --> 00:03:14.485
by 15% and doubled
the number of Pell-grant

00:03:14.485 --> 00:03:17.488
eligible and first
generation college students.

00:03:17.989 --> 00:03:22.994
Along the way, we've raised over
$5 billion through the

00:03:22.994 --> 00:03:26.414
For Humanity campaign
toward the $7 billion goal.

00:03:26.414 --> 00:03:28.833
And I'm not going to stop
fundraising,

00:03:28.833 --> 00:03:31.252
even after
returning to the faculty.

00:03:31.252 --> 00:03:33.922
You can read more about what
we have accomplished together

00:03:33.922 --> 00:03:38.468
over the past ten years in the
accompanying Yale News story.

00:03:39.135 --> 00:03:42.138
Of course, our work is not done.

00:03:42.138 --> 00:03:44.223
We have a busy year ahead.

00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:47.477
I look forward to working with
you on research

00:03:47.477 --> 00:03:49.896
and educational programs
and initiatives

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:54.359
that support faculty, students,
staff, and alumni.

00:03:54.359 --> 00:03:57.612
And we will continue to move
ahead on the planned investments

00:03:57.612 --> 00:04:01.616
in various schools and units,
such as the expansion of faculty

00:04:01.616 --> 00:04:04.285
facilities projects,
whether in planning

00:04:04.285 --> 00:04:07.914
or construction phases
throughout the university.

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:10.750
Our partnership
with the City of New Haven;

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.962
and well-being
and Belonging Initiatives.

00:04:13.962 --> 00:04:16.631
In the meantime, I want to
thank you for your partnership

00:04:16.631 --> 00:04:20.510
over the years and for
your commitment to Yale.

